    {
      "id": "claim_3586063d313f4d1a98b969e16f99a55a",
      "statement": "celld records a span for each stateless Worker request, each cell event (fetch, alarm, RPC, WebSocket message), each outbound fetch(), and each cell start, carrying request id, cell, isolate, queue wait, outbound URL and status, and durability facts; each console.log line becomes a log record carrying the trace id and span id of the writing handler so queries can join logs to traces, surviving await.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L36-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42c5ac83cdad9698ac1b302dc067a9c8912351f3e9a5ec2ec60f6162fed47c2d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e5fdc8c9669043c48733e403d2185f13",
      "statement": "A console.log body larger than LOG_BODY_CAP (8 KiB) is truncated, because log records are telemetry rather than blob storage and one runaway line must not dominate a batch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L38-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:900f26655857289229c4951e1a13fca54a42712152dc1fac110770af243198ed:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_293f3ba7b1aa4a8f9dd0a2cdfa6f63ab",
      "statement": "Trace interop: celld reads the W3C traceparent header on incoming requests so its spans join the upstream trace, sends traceparent on outbound fetch(), keeps a Worker call to a Durable Object in one trace, and records no metrics yet — the spans carry durations and queue waits.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L49-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5865356011a464c4978e8d6be53dff590b7fa2c32fa53b0a9cd422e323f8dbca:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f5eb6f3ff5a04ef8b60c02b8757c89a0",
      "statement": "Internally a channel of capacity 8192 sits between the hot path and the pump: a full queue sheds (counted), and the pump drains continuously with size-triggered batching so the channel only needs to cover a scheduling hiccup rather than a full flush interval.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L47-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:73a2070453b0ecae6d506616523668bc86ee0d1ee7ae729a1b0d226f02258955:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c1dd6d0dde84467c82021ee85f067a84",
      "statement": "Sampling: the sampler decides at request start; an unsampled request records nothing and costs almost nothing; under load telemetry sheds before requests do and celld counts what it sheds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L54-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:806f80227d453f075483312f4d4a07c76055d508b4356b4e2c7dfc00f10bfb9c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
